{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987847-knocking-someone-down","id":987847,"title":"Knocking Someone Down?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-15T11:15:23-07:00","id":987847,"title":"Knocking Someone Down?","content":"After reading over the Knocked Down Tilt I am confused as to how how one actually inflicts the Tilt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Causing the Tilt:</b> Some weapons list \u201cKnockdown\u201d as a special effect of a damaging hit. Otherwise, a melee weapon with a damage modifier of +2 or greater, or a firearm with a damage modifier of +3 or more can be used to knock a character down with the force of the blow. Alternatively, a melee weapon or unarmed attack can knock an opponent down with a targeted attack against the legs (\u20132 modifier). The attacker declares that he wants to knock his opponent down and halves the total damage done (rounding down). On a successful attack, the target is knocked down. </div> </div> </div>Does this mean that Melee Weapons with +2 or greater damage modifiers &amp; Firearms with +3 Damage or more automatically deal out Knocked Down Tilts to those hit with them?<br /> <br /> Is there a Knock Down Maneuver somewhere that I am missing? If so please post me some page numbers to reference<br /> <br /> As I am reading the Tilt is sounds like Melee Weapons that do +2 Damage or more and Firearms that do +3 Damage or more automatically Knock People Down, and that if you use a weapon that does less damage you need to target the legs and either do enough damage to each leg to inflict two separate leg wracks or target the legs with intent to Knock Down and only do half damage.<br /> <br /> I guess my real confusion is how do Melee weapons +2 Damage and Firearms +3 Damage Knock targets down with the Force of the Blow.<br /> <br /> Thank you for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4630-jmecha","name":"JMecha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:03:08-07:00","id":987870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JMecha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/987847-knocking-someone-down#post987847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does this mean that Melee Weapons with +2 or greater damage modifiers &amp; Firearms with +3 Damage or more automatically deal out Knocked Down Tilts to those hit with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe in this case you declare you're going to try to knock them down with the attack, then do half damage. If you succeed in your attack, your damage is halved as per the declaration, and the target is knocked down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there a Knock Down Maneuver somewhere that I am missing? If so please post me some page numbers to reference </div> </div> </div>There's a couple in Fighting Styles. Kick 'Em While They're Down and Like the Breeze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:57:01-07:00","id":987898,"title":"","content":"Knocking someone down with a weapon that does not have the Knockdown quality always requires you to declare intent to knock the target down before the attack roll, and halves the damage done on a successful hit. If the weapon has less than a +2 modifier (or +3 modifier for Firearms), you <i>also</i> have to target the legs, imposing a -2 penalty to the attack roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 10-15-2016, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T17:05:48-07:00","id":988012,"title":"","content":"I believe the confusion stems from reading the first statement as one way to cause the tilt, and the second and third sentence together as the second way. Instead the first and second sentences describes two different conditions that allows the tilt to be caused, and the third sentence is what you need to do to cause it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}